out.push(h2('7.7  Review & Mediate: One cause, two symptoms'));
out.push(S('Stage 1 · Get ready – Unit 7 quiz'));
out.push(A('**1** _The bead is thin, **which** in turn leaves the clips carrying the load._   **2** _…with the result **that** the bead varies._   **3** _Five of the seven are attributable **to** a fourth night._   **4** _The fourth night **accounts** for about five of the seven._   **5** _A bed moved at three in the morning is **a trigger**: it explains the timing._   **6** _Which **predicts** that the afternoon runs will be repeated more often._'));
out.push(A('⚠ Items **3** and **4** are the two that catch everybody and they are both prepositions: _attributable **to**_ and _accounts **for**_. Item **5** is the only one that is not a grammar error at all — the sentence is perfectly formed and says something false — and it is the one to spend the time on, because **it is the error the whole unit is about** and no proof-reader will ever find it.'));
out.push(S('Stage 2 · Listen and read'));
out.push(A('**a** Open — the two complaints are read as they arrived, with the twelve-word record under them and the repeat log under that.'));
out.push(A('**b** They have **one cause** in common and neither party can see the other\'s symptom. And a mediator must show **what each party is already doing about their own symptom, and why both of those will fail.**'));
out.push(NOTE('⚠ **This is the third mediation of the course and it is a third kind, which is worth saying to the class in those words.** In **4.7** both parties had overclaimed and the mediator put each at its honest step. In **6.7** the record was silent and the mediator named what it did say. **Here both parties are reading one document correctly and the document is defective** — so there is nothing to decide, nobody to correct, and the mediator\'s third move is new: **show each party\'s own remedy and why it will fail.** ⚠ The sentence to put on the board is the one about the better remedy: the afternoon bench has spent four hours a month since September making its own symptom legible, which is more than the clinicians have done, **and a successful symptom remedy is the more dangerous of the two because it buys patience with the cause.** And the removal test is what proves there is one cause and not two: **remove the candidate and _both_ symptoms must stop.** If only one stops, the class is mediating the wrong thing.'));
out.push(S('Language box · Practise'));
