out.push(A('⚠ On **Pair B** the arithmetic is the same in a different trade. The printer\'s symptom is setting the contents page twice; the contributors\' symptom is having their worked-on paragraphs cut. **The one cause is a style sheet that says _open with the subject of the paragraph_ and names no author**, so the contents page is written from an opening that was written to a rule nobody owns. Remove it and both stop. **The settling thing already exists: the contents lines for six issues, beside the paragraphs they describe.** And both local remedies fail in the same way — the printer sets the page twice and the contributors write longer openings.'));
out.push(S('Stage 3R · Perform – listener task'));
out.push(A('The two symptoms, the one cause and the two failing remedies for each pair. The count: **about half the mediators name two causes rather than one** and have to be sent back to the removal test. ⚠ And in **both** pairs the cause is a phrase in a document with **no author** — _where applicable_, _open with the subject_ — which is 6.4 arriving inside Unit 7 and is worth naming, because it means the two units\' habits work on the same documents.'));
